{"name":"Nightshade","hex":"#3c464b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nightshade","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the poisonous plants belonging to the genus Solanum, especially black nightshade or woody nightshade.","Any plant of the wider Solanaceae family, including the nightshades as well as tomato, potato, eggplant, and deadly nightshade."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nightshade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nightshade (DC Comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Nightshade is a superhero appearing in American comic books published by DC Comics. Created by David Kaler and Steve Ditko, the character first appeared in Captain Atom #82 originally published by Charlton Comics."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nightshade_(DC_Comics)","wikidata":"Q3876803"},{"title":"Nightshade (2003 video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Nightshade is a 2003 action-adventure game developed by Sega AM1 and published by Sega for the PlayStation 2. It is the eleventh game in the Shinobi series and follows the exploits of a female ninja named Hibana. The game is a sequel to the 2002 PlayStation 2 game, Shinobi, although it focuses on a new set of characters and a separated plot line."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/ba/Nightshade_%28PS2%29_Coverart.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nightshade_(2003_video_game)","wikidata":"Q2344305"},{"title":"Solanaceae","blocks":[{"text":"Solanaceae, commonly known as the nightshades, is a family of flowering plants in the order Solanales. The family contains approximately 2,700 species, several of which are used as agricultural crops, medicinal plants, and ornamental plants. Many members of the family have high alkaloid contents, making some highly toxic, but many—such as tomatoes, potatoes, eggplants and peppers—are commonly used in food around the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Brugmansia_lg.jpg/330px-Brugmansia_lg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solanaceae","wikidata":"Q134172"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d5/Nightshade_%28Charlton_Comics%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d5/Nightshade_%28Charlton_Comics%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANightshade_(Charlton_Comics).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Captain_Atom_82.jpg/500px-Captain_Atom_82.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Captain_Atom_82.jpg/1280px-Captain_Atom_82.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Captain_Atom_82.jpg/500px-Captain_Atom_82.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Nightshade (right) on the cover of Captain Atom #82, art by Steve Ditko.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACaptain_Atom_82.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/31/Incnightshade.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/31/Incnightshade.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Nightshade in Suicide Squad #17 (June 1988), art by Luke McDonnell.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIncnightshade.png"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9d/Nightshade_%28DC_Comics_2018%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://up